tion  about the state of the opposition  they're a reflection of the success of  the vaccination program and people  feeling maybe maybe maybe we're just  coming out of this  this hell they're also a reflection of  the fact that i think the media  does not hold this government to account  nor does parliament frankly  does not hold this government to account  in the way that they should i think the  media has become incredibly supine in  its coverage of the government  and even on the coming stuff yes  wall-to-wall coverage  but then by the weekend it's oh well who  cares what dominic cummings think the  sun's shining  vaccination program is going well  johnson's got married let's just move on  and i think the country's just got to  decide do we care  about the fact that we have a government  and a prime minister that has comings  and i agree with him this  they are directly responsible for tens  of thousands of deaths do we care about  that or not  do we care that a prime minister stands  up in parliament you've now got that  video from peter stevanovic  over 20 million views hardly anybody in  the mainstream media covering it  where they set out we talk about has he  broken the ministerial code he breaks  the ministerial code virtually every  time he stands up in parliament they're  meant to tell the truth  and this is what populism has done to  our politics  i we could talk about um your views uh  about uh this this government forever  and  you know you know i you've been pretty  clear let's let's put it that way  on that but let's just uh talk about  some of the underlying substantive  questions here some of the ones that  i've talked  i was talking to bob kerslaker about  about the nature of government because  you've been inside it  one new labour minister complained why i  think while you were still  there that he thought that when you got  into government  there was this great machine and you're  if you're a minister  you pull a lever and the machine whirs  i