  know you say you  they did terrific job in some respects  they weren't always that complimentary  about you  i mean i heard a former cabinet  secretary on the radio this week  saying that some of the roth set in with  the sofa government  of the blair regime and you were one of  the people on the sofa  uh some of the people in whitehall would  say this is all  your fault well i don't know who that  was and  and i think that the whole thing about  sofa government is it was just a  complete  nonsense tony blair ran a very tight  ship  and he embraced the civil service i  remember one of the first things he did  was took me and jonathan powell into a  room  jonathan who was the other special  adviser who was a was we were given  these  special dispensations to instruct civil  servants and he was very very clear we  work with these people we don't work  against them  and i think you'd find very very few  people who worked with me  or with jonathan powell or any of the  others who were in there one of the  things i'm  most proud of actually is the people  nobody who's ever worked for me in the  civil service  has ever come out and criticized the way  that we dealt with them  and the way that we worked with them and  you know i think the other point bob  made  very quickly gone can i guide you one  other question sorry  of course which is about the the effect  of the last year  there have been stories this week about  effect of on people's mental health and  i know this is something that  you are particularly uh concerned about  if you've got any thoughts about  what we ought to be think doing going  forward  well i am really worried about this  because i i understand that the  government has  you know its main focus has been on in  dealing with the pandemic  but you know the royal college of  psychiatrist has warned about mental  illness being the  the second pandemic and you know that  whether that overstates it or not i  think we all know  that there are going to be 